.TH NOSTR-HOMED-PROVISION-STATUS 1 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-homed-provision-status \- inspect porthome-status.json for an arbitrary home
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-homed-provision status
[\fB\-\-home\fR \fIDIR\fR | \fB\-\-uid\fR \fIUID\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-field\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-path\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads
.I <home>/.local/state/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
and pretty-prints it, dumps it as raw JSON, or extracts a single scalar
field. Home resolution is either explicit via
.B \-\-home\ DIR
or via
.BR getpwuid (3)
lookup with
.BR \-\-uid\ UID .
.PP
This command has the same schema as
.BR nostr-home-status (1),
but is intended for the operator case where the caller wants to inspect
another user's home (e.g. from a support script running as root).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-home \fIDIR\fR
Use DIR as the home root. The status file is expected at
.IR DIR/.local/state/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json .
.TP
.B \-\-uid \fIUID\fR
Resolve the home via
.BR getpwuid (3).
Requires the caller to have libnss access to the target uid's entry.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the file verbatim as JSON on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-field \fIPATH\fR
Print a single scalar, using the same dotted syntax as
.BR nostr-home-status (1)
(e.g.
.IR syncd.state ,
.IR fuse.mounted ,
.IR provisioner.last_push ).
Exit 1 if the field is missing.
.TP
.B \-\-path
Print the resolved status file path and exit. Useful for scripts.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Success (status file read and requested output emitted).
.TP 4
.B 1
Malformed JSON, or
.B \-\-field
matched no key.
.TP 4
.B 2
Bad argument (both
.BR \-\-home " and " \-\-uid ,
or neither).
.TP 4
.B 3
Status file does not exist. Distinguish from exit 1 because a missing file
usually means the target home is not managed by porthome, not a bug.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Pretty-print the current user's syncd state:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision status \-\-home ~ \-\-field syncd.state
.fi
.RE
.PP
Machine-readable dump of another user's status:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo nostr-homed-provision status \-\-uid 1001 \-\-json | jq .
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <home>/.local/state/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
Status file. Written by
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8),
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8),
and
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1)
itself.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-home-status (1),
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
